From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] proximity: drop invalid states without terminating the client

Keep the existing near/far contract and free every decoded message. An unknown
integer must not abort SensorProxy. Validate the Davinci float before any
conversion so fractional, non-finite and out-of-range input cannot become a
false near/far report or undefined float-to-integer conversion.

Reviewed against libssc v0.4.4 and upstream main
4e4c6c8cc702a754bd700506c01961aaf971a23b. No Uke calibration, protocol field
or board setting is introduced. Existing GPL-3.0-or-later attribution remains.

Signed-off-by: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/src/libssc-sensor-proximity.c
+++ b/src/libssc-sensor-proximity.c
@@ -89,16 +89,12 @@
 				return;
 			}
 
-			switch (msg->near) {
-				case SSC_SENSOR_PROXIMITY_NEAR:
-					near = true;
-					break;
-				case SSC_SENSOR_PROXIMITY_FAR:
-					near = false;
-					break;
-				default:
-					g_assert_not_reached ();
+			if (msg->near != SSC_SENSOR_PROXIMITY_NEAR && msg->near != SSC_SENSOR_PROXIMITY_FAR) {
+				ssc_proximity_response__free_unpacked (msg, NULL);
+				g_warning ("Invalid proximity state");
+				return;
 			}
+			near = msg->near == SSC_SENSOR_PROXIMITY_NEAR;
 
 			ssc_proximity_response__free_unpacked (msg, NULL);
 		/* xiaomi-davinci uses REPORT_MEASUREMENT and its own proximity response */
@@ -120,16 +116,12 @@
 
 			memcpy(&data, msg->data->data, sizeof(ProximityDataDavinci));
 
-			switch ((int)data.near) {
-				case SSC_SENSOR_PROXIMITY_NEAR:
-					near = true;
-					break;
-				case SSC_SENSOR_PROXIMITY_FAR:
-					near = false;
-					break;
-				default:
-					g_assert_not_reached ();
+			if (data.near != SSC_SENSOR_PROXIMITY_NEAR && data.near != SSC_SENSOR_PROXIMITY_FAR) {
+				ssc_proximity_response_davinci__free_unpacked (msg, NULL);
+				g_warning ("Invalid Xiaomi Davinci proximity state");
+				return;
 			}
+			near = data.near == SSC_SENSOR_PROXIMITY_NEAR;
 
 			ssc_proximity_response_davinci__free_unpacked (msg, NULL);
 		} else {
